\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Satellite E-class morphology versus median projected pair separation \(\langle R_{ij}\rangle \). \textit  {(a)} The upper histograms show the fraction of CG\textsubscript  {4}{} and Control\textsubscript  {4C}{} quartets per 0.1-dex bin, each normalised to its own sample, with dotted lines at their medians (143 and 293~kpc). The lower panel shows E-class fractions among E/S satellites in 0.2-dex bins and sample-specific logistic fits, both at \(\log _{10}(M_\star /\mathrm  {M}_\odot )=10.20\); RG\textsubscript  {4}{} is shown for reference only and enters no contrast. Bars give 95\% intervals; bins with fewer than three physical hosts are omitted, and the two bins below 100~kpc rest on few CG\textsubscript  {4}{} hosts (Sect.~\ref {sec:morphology}). Grey marks the shared range (94--219~kpc). \textit  {(b)} The separate-slope CG\textsubscript  {4}{} minus Control\textsubscript  {4C}{} contrast averages multivariable predictions over the CG\textsubscript  {4}{} satellites within \(\pm 0.1\)~dex of each separation that have a Control\textsubscript  {4C}{} counterpart (Appendix~\ref {app:stat_conventions}). The circle marks the estimate at 150~kpc; its bar and the ribbon give pointwise 95\% intervals. The right part gives the full-sample contrast and the separation matches without and with a \(120\,\mathrm  {km\,s}^{-1}\) velocity-dispersion tolerance (Table~\ref {tab:group_match_per_control}). A raw-fraction variant is deposited on Zenodo (\textbf  {[ZENODO DOI TO BE INSERTED]}).}}{7}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:compactness}{{3}{7}{Satellite E-class morphology versus median projected pair separation \(\Rmed \). \textit {(a)} The upper histograms show the fraction of \CG {} and \CC {} quartets per 0.1-dex bin, each normalised to its own sample, with dotted lines at their medians (143 and 293~kpc). The lower panel shows E-class fractions among E/S satellites in 0.2-dex bins and sample-specific logistic fits, both at \(\log _{10}(M_\star /\msun )=10.20\); \RG {} is shown for reference only and enters no contrast. Bars give 95\% intervals; bins with fewer than three physical hosts are omitted, and the two bins below 100~kpc rest on few \CG {} hosts (Sect.~\ref {sec:morphology}). Grey marks the shared range (94--219~kpc). \textit {(b)} The separate-slope \CG {} minus \CC {} contrast averages multivariable predictions over the \CG {} satellites within \(\pm 0.1\)~dex of each separation that have a \CC {} counterpart (Appendix~\ref {app:stat_conventions}). The circle marks the estimate at 150~kpc; its bar and the ribbon give pointwise 95\% intervals. The right part gives the full-sample contrast and the separation matches without and with a \(120\kms \) velocity-dispersion tolerance (Table~\ref {tab:group_match_per_control}). A raw-fraction variant is deposited on Zenodo (\zenodoDOI )}{figure.3}{}}
