\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {B.1}{\ignorespaces Galaxy Zoo morphology in sSFR--stellar-mass space for the SDSS non-AGN reference. Panels show the E, S, and uncertain classes. Solid contours (red for E, blue for S, and grey for uncertain) enclose 20, 40, 60, 80, and 95\% of the density after display-only Gaussian smoothing with \(\sigma =1.25\) histogram bins; grey dotted contours show the smoothed full reference distribution, and the dashed curve is the unchanged adopted GMM boundary. The star-forming lobe in the E-class panel reflects low-mass galaxies in the flux-limited SDSS reference (\(r \le 17.77\)), where compact or unresolved galaxies can receive smooth votes. The panel titles count the reference galaxies of each class with a valid sSFR, hence differ from Table~\ref {tab:morphologies}. The group samples lie mostly at higher stellar masses (\(\log (M_\star /\mathrm  {M}_\odot ) \gtrsim 9.5\)), and the quenched locus dominates their E class (Table~\ref {tab:quenched_by_morphology}).}}{13}{figure.B.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:sSFR_classification}{{B.1}{13}{Galaxy Zoo morphology in sSFR--stellar-mass space for the SDSS non-AGN reference. Panels show the E, S, and uncertain classes. Solid contours (red for E, blue for S, and grey for uncertain) enclose 20, 40, 60, 80, and 95\% of the density after display-only Gaussian smoothing with \(\sigma =1.25\) histogram bins; grey dotted contours show the smoothed full reference distribution, and the dashed curve is the unchanged adopted GMM boundary. The star-forming lobe in the E-class panel reflects low-mass galaxies in the flux-limited SDSS reference (\(r \le 17.77\)), where compact or unresolved galaxies can receive smooth votes. The panel titles count the reference galaxies of each class with a valid sSFR, hence differ from Table~\ref {tab:morphologies}. The group samples lie mostly at higher stellar masses (\(\log (M_\star /\msun ) \gtrsim 9.5\)), and the quenched locus dominates their E class (Table~\ref {tab:quenched_by_morphology})}{figure.B.1}{}}
